---

## 📘 **Conjunction (संयोजक) क्या होता है?**

**Conjunctions** वे शब्द होते हैं जो **दो या दो से अधिक शब्दों, वाक्यांशों (phrases) या वाक्यों (sentences)** को आपस में जोड़ते हैं।

🔹 **Definition in English**:
*A conjunction is a word used to connect words, phrases, or clauses.*

---

## 🧩 **Types of Conjunctions (संयोजकों के प्रकार)**

### 1. **Coordinating Conjunctions** (समन्वयक संयोजक)

ये समान श्रेणी के दो भागों को जोड़ते हैं – जैसे शब्द, वाक्यांश, या स्वतंत्र उपवाक्य।

📚 **FANBOYS** = **For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So**

| Conjunction | Use (प्रयोग)     | Example                                   |
| ----------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **For**     | कारण             | He was tired, **for** he worked all day.  |
| **And**     | जोड़ने के लिए    | She likes apples **and** bananas.         |
| **Nor**     | नकारात्मक विकल्प | He does not smoke, **nor** does he drink. |
| **But**     | विरोध            | I want to go, **but** I am busy.          |
| **Or**      | विकल्प           | Tea **or** coffee?                        |
| **Yet**     | फिर भी           | He is old, **yet** strong.                |
| **So**      | परिणाम           | It was raining, **so** I stayed home.     |

---

### 2. **Subordinating Conjunctions** (आधीन संयोजक)

ये मुख्य वाक्य (main clause) को अधीन वाक्य (subordinate clause) से जोड़ते हैं।

🔸 **अर्थ के अनुसार उपवर्ग**:

| Use                    | Conjunctions                                   | Examples                          |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |
| **Time (समय)**         | when, while, before, after, since, till, until | I stayed **until** he came.       |
| **Reason (कारण)**      | because, as, since                             | She left **because** it was late. |
| **Purpose (उद्देश्य)** | so that, in order that                         | Study hard **so that** you pass.  |
| **Condition (शर्त)**   | if, unless, provided that                      | You can go **if** you finish.     |
| **Contrast (विरोध)**   | though, although, even though                  | **Though** it was cold, he went.  |
| **Comparison**         | as...as, than                                  | He is taller **than** me.         |
| **Place (स्थान)**      | where, wherever                                | Go **where** you want.            |

---

### 3. **Correlative Conjunctions** (युग्म संयोजक)

ये जोड़े में आते हैं और दोनों ओर एक जैसे पदों को जोड़ते हैं।

| Correlative Pair        | Example                                           |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| **Either...or**         | **Either** you go **or** stay.                    |
| **Neither...nor**       | **Neither** John **nor** his friends came.        |
| **Both...and**          | **Both** Ram **and** Shyam are intelligent.       |
| **Not only...but also** | **Not only** she sings, **but also** dances.      |
| **Whether...or**        | I don’t know **whether** he will come **or** not. |
| **Such...that**         | He is **such** a fool **that** no one listens.    |

---

## 📌 **Common Uses of Conjunctions**

| Purpose            | Example                             |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| दो शब्द जोड़ना     | He is smart **and** clever.         |
| दो वाक्यांश जोड़ना | I want to eat **but** not now.      |
| दो उपवाक्य जोड़ना  | He came **after** I called him.     |
| विकल्प दिखाना      | You may take tea **or** coffee.     |
| शर्त बताना         | I will come **if** it doesn’t rain. |
| विरोध/कंट्रास्ट    | He worked hard, **yet** he failed.  |

---

## ✅ **Quick Summary Table of Common Conjunctions**

| Type              | Examples                                                            |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Coordinating**  | and, but, or, so, yet, for, nor                                     |
| **Subordinating** | because, if, when, although, unless, since, while, till, as soon as |
| **Correlative**   | either...or, neither...nor, both...and, not only...but also         |

